  "tarball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/feder-cr/jev/tarball/jevos-v5",
  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/feder-cr/jev/zipball/jevos-v5",
  "body": "Yes/no decisions on a laptop CPU in 28\u2013130 ms: `jev`, one binary for Windows, Linux and macOS, now with **jevos-v5** at 8-bit weights. 78.9% on the benchmark's headline yes/no sets and 74.0% on agent instructions (DynaBench); choices 73.5%, scores 48.3%. On the 999 hand-written yes/no questions it gets 79.6%, on held-out rules 88.8%.\n\nQuestions asked in the negative (#44), such as \"Is this not about X?\", are now read as negated: on 1,398 plain and negated questions written for that issue, jevos-v5 gets 96.7% of the negated ones right and 99.0% of the plain ones. It was trained on negated questions written the same way, so this checks the fix. Public negation sets test something else, a negation inside the text: there it gets 61.7% on CondaQA and 74.1% on the negation NLI sets of Hossain et al., behind larger models.\n\nWhere it is weaker: the support cases of typed_decisions (yes/no 64.7%) and PubMedQA (70.4%); it is also fairly confident when a needed fact is missing from a rated policy. Check it on your own questions before relying on it.\n\njevos-v5 is a training run of the 17-layer model on a wide mix: policies, records and contract excerpts written as natural text, and yes/no questions asked in the negative; a short second pass on the natural-text part was then averaged with the first run. Measured through `jev` itself (OpenVINO INT8).\n\nDownload the archive for your system and the model, and unpack the model into the `jev` folder:\n\n```bash\ntar -xzf jev-linux-x64.tar.gz                 # Windows: unzip jev-windows-x64.zip\ncd jev\nunzip ../jevos-v5-openvino-int8.zip           # creates model/\n./jev serve                                   # Windows: jev.exe serve\n```\n\n| File | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `jev-windows-x64.zip`, `jev-linux-x64.tar.gz` (glibc 2.35+), `jev-macos-arm64.tar.gz` | the `jev` binary with OpenVINO's libraries and the licenses |\n| `jevos-v5-openvino-int8.zip` | the model `jev` runs, as `model/` |\n| `jevos-v5-q4_k_m.gguf`, `jevos-v5-q8_0.gguf` | the same model as GGUF, for llama.cpp and the tools built on it |\n| `SHA256SUMS.txt` | the SHA-256 of every file here |\n\nThe API, options and numbers are in the [README](https://github.com/feder-cr/jev#readme).\n"
}
